      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Construction lumber is the basic wood material used to build various structures. It generally includes boards that are 2 to 4 inches thick and 2 to 12 inches wide. It comes in different grades and wood species. Lumber is a sustainable and environmentally friendly construction material that could replace traditional building materials. Its structural performance, capacity to fixate CO2 and low energy demand during the manufacturing process make it an interesting material. Carpenters use softwood to construct inner structures and furniture.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "建筑木材是用于建造各种结构的基本木质材料。一般包括 2 到 4 英寸厚、2 到 12 英寸宽的木板。它有不同的等级和木种。木材是一种可替代传统建筑材料的可持续环保建筑材料。它的结构性能、固定二氧化碳的能力和制造过程中的低能耗需求使其成为一种有趣的材料。木匠使用软木建造内部结构和家具。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
